   "project": "fieldnotes",
   "reply": "I added `fieldnotes export`, which prints one `DATE: TEXT` line per note. `python tools/check.py` passes: both tests (the existing one and the new one) succeed, and the line-length check is clean.\n\n- **Store:** `fieldnotes/store.py` has a new `export_lines()` that builds the lines, so it can be tested without the CLI.\n- **CLI:** `fieldnotes/cli.py` handles `export` and prints each line. I moved the usage message into a shared `USAGE` constant that now lists `export`.\n- **Test:** `tests/test_store.py` has a new `test_export_lines`, which checks two notes come out as `2026-01-02: first` and `2026-02-03: second`.\n\n- **Date format:** I used just the day from each note's timestamp (`2026-01-02`), not the full ISO timestamp. If you want the full timestamp, change the slice in `export_lines()`.\n- **Test coverage:** The CLI `export` branch itself has no test. The test covers `export_lines()` only.\n- **Check setup:** `tools/check.py` needs `NOTES_HOME` set and it wasn't, so I ran it with `NOTES_HOME` pointing at a fresh temp directory.",
